+      <p class="eyebrow">Recent releases</p>
+      <h2>What's new since v9.3.0</h2>
+      <p class="sub">Every one of these started as a field report from a real device.</p>
       <div class="grid g2">
-        <div class="card"><span class="ico">🩺</span><h3>Repair that tells the truth</h3><p>On Android shared storage (FUSE/sdcardfs) a damaged <code>.git</code> used to die at the atomic swap with a silent <code>[FAIL]</code>. Now: the <em>actual</em> <code>mv</code> error is printed, and when the filesystem can't do atomic renames of directories, ob-sync switches to a copy-based install automatically — with a timestamped pre-repair backup taken either way.</p></div>
-        <div class="card"><span class="ico">🚀</span><h3>Init joins the menu</h3><p>First-time setup is no longer CLI-only. Menu option <code>18) Init</code> keeps or changes the vault path, asks for the new remote URL, then runs <code>git init</code> with additive history alignment — or clones a fresh vault when the directory is empty. The same battle-tested flow, now where phone users actually live.</p></div>
